.venv/
# Without the slash-less form, a `.venv` SYMLINK is not ignored: a trailing
# slash matches directories only, and git treats a symlink as a file. Parallel
# worktrees symlink the main checkout's venv rather than building their own
# (scripts/dev/worktree-spawn.sh), so every such worktree showed `.venv` as
# untracked — one `git add -A` away from committing an absolute path to one
# developer's machine.
.venv
venv
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

